From 8a4a7e8fe426692da822390a398454c989465510 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeltaTor <deltator@example.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:31:32 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 40/40] conflux: add a warm-up re-measurement interval for the
 probe

Add ConfluxProbeWarmupInterval. While a set's first ConfluxProbeInterval is
still running, its throughput estimate is now refreshed at most every
ConfluxProbeWarmupInterval seconds instead of only when the full first window
has elapsed, so the measured-throughput policies can start adapting shortly
after startup.

Each early refresh deliberately uses the cumulative delivered bytes and active
time since the window opened, not the short slice since the previous refresh: a
few seconds of traffic are too noisy to trust on their own, and the point of
the warm-up is to give selection an early but already-stable estimate. The
baseline and the window start are not advanced, so the first normal roll still
measures the whole first ConfluxProbeInterval, after which the previous rolling
logic continues unchanged.

The warm-up never decays an estimate; a set that has not yet moved
ConfluxProbeMinBytes simply keeps its previous value. It is off by default (0),
so existing behaviour is unchanged.
