+[[ConfluxProbeWarmupInterval]] **ConfluxProbeWarmupInterval** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: early re-measurement interval, in seconds, for
+    ConfluxSetSelection 4 and 5. Until a set's first ConfluxProbeInterval has
+    elapsed, its throughput estimate is refreshed at most this often instead of
+    waiting for the full first window, so selection starts adapting sooner.
+    Each early refresh uses the cumulative delivered bytes and active time since
+    the window opened, not the short slice since the previous refresh, so a few
+    seconds of data are never trusted on their own. Once the full
+    ConfluxProbeInterval has elapsed the normal per-window measurement takes
+    over. 0 disables the warm-up. It only has an effect when it is smaller than
+    ConfluxProbeInterval. Valid range: 0-3600. (Default: 0)
+
 [[ConfluxProbeMinBytes]] **ConfluxProbeMinBytes** __NUM__::
     DeltaTor extension: minimum delivered bytes a conflux set must move inside
     one ConfluxProbeInterval window before its throughput estimate is trusted.
